{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-77626-r4615154","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Khatti Dal (Spiced Tamarind Pigeon Peas)","sourcePageId":77626,"sourceRevision":"4615154","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:26:51Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Khatti%20Dal%20(Spiced%20Tamarind%20Pigeon%20Peas)&oldid=4615154","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:07:10.350Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Legume recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes for dal","Category:Recipes using cilantro","Category:Recipes using curry leaf","Category:Recipes using ginger paste","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes using whole cumin","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:South Asian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"2d19e4a0ccd0869ae343df323f208ae0d111723d096e059df7e3f47b8d003e80","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = South Asian recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:South Asian cuisines|South Asian cuisines]]\n\nThis is a variety of dal, the common staple food of South Asia made with [[Cookbook:Dal|dal]] forming a stew or thick soup. Dal is the name for split [[Cookbook:Legume|legumes]] in many South Asian languages (see [[Cookbook:Dal|dal]] page). Khatti translates as sour from Hindi, and comes from the use of tamarind, a very sour fruit on its own. Serve with any variety of [[Cookbook:Roti|roti]] (a round flat bread) or over rice and with a vegetable preparation on the side and an achar (pickle) or chutney as condiments. The roti is used to scoop up the dal and grab pieces of the vegetable.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (240 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) [[Cookbook:Pigeon Pea|toor]] [[Cookbook:Dal|daal]] (split pigeon peas)\n*2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger paste]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic paste]]\n*3 tbsp [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] or crushed [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]]\n*6–8 pieces whole [[Cookbook:Tamarind|tamarind]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Chili Powder|red chilli powder]]\n*½ tsp [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard seeds]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin seeds]] (jeera)\n*[[Cookbook:Curry Leaf|Curry leaves]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n*[[Cookbook:Cilantro|Coriander leaves]] (cilantro) for garnish\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Wash toor daal and [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] for about 20 minutes until soft. Drain and smash the dal.\n# In a [[Cookbook:Kadai|kadai]], heat the oil until hot. Add curry leaves, mustard seeds and jeera seeds. [[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] for a minute. They will pop at first, so a cover will help to avoid a mess.\n# Add onion and fry until slightly brown.\n# Add ginger and garlic paste. Fry for a minute, then add the tomatoes. Cook until the oil separates.\n# Add tamarind pieces, turmeric powder, and red chilli powder. Cook it for 4–5 minutes.\n# Add the toor daal and enough water for your desired thickness.\n# Add salt to taste, and [[Cookbook:Garnish|garnish]] with coriander leaves.\n# Serve with a roti or poured over rice.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for curry|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:South Asian recipes|Khatti Dal]]\n[[Category:Legume recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cilantro]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dal]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ginger paste]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whole cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Khatti Dal (Spiced Tamarind Pigeon Peas)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup (240 ml) toor daal (split pigeon peas)","sourceText":"1 cup (240 ml) toor daal (split pigeon peas)","amountText":"1 cup (240 ml) toor daal (split pigeon peas)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tbsp oil","sourceText":"2 tbsp oil","amountText":"2 tbsp oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 onion","sourceText":"1 onion","amountText":"1 onion","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ tsp ginger paste","sourceText":"½ tsp ginger paste","amountText":"½ tsp ginger paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 tsp garlic paste","sourceText":"1 tsp garlic paste","amountText":"1 tsp garlic paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"3 tbsp diced or crushed tomato","sourceText":"3 tbsp diced or crushed tomato","amountText":"3 tbsp diced or crushed tomato","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"6–8 pieces whole tamarind","sourceText":"6–8 pieces whole tamarind","amountText":"6–8 pieces whole tamarind","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"1 tsp red chilli powder","sourceText":"1 tsp red chilli powder","amountText":"1 tsp red chilli powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"½ tsp turmeric","sourceText":"½ tsp turmeric","amountText":"½ ts